---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import stats from '../data/stats.json';
---

<BaseLayout title="Home" fullBleed>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <h1>LocalBoundaries of Nepal</h1>
      <p class="hero-tagline">
        Open, reusable administrative boundary data for Nepal's provinces, districts, and local
        levels, in GeoJSON, TopoJSON, Shapefile, KML, and GeoPackage.
      </p>
      <form class="hero-search" action="/download/" method="get">
        <input type="search" name="q" placeholder="Search a province, district, or local level&hellip;" aria-label="Search boundary data" />
        <button type="submit">Search</button>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stat-tiles">
    <div class="stat-tile">
      <span class="stat-number">{stats.provinces}</span>
      <span class="stat-label">Provinces</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-tile">
      <span class="stat-number">{stats.districts}</span>
      <span class="stat-label">Districts</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-tile">
      <span class="stat-number">{stats.metropolitan}</span>
      <span class="stat-label">Metropolitan Cities</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-tile">
      <span class="stat-number">{stats.sub_metropolitan}</span>
      <span class="stat-label">Sub-Metropolitan Cities</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-tile">
      <span class="stat-number">{stats.municipality}</span>
      <span class="stat-label">Municipalities</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-tile">
      <span class="stat-number">{stats.rural_municipality}</span>
      <span class="stat-label">Rural Municipalities</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-tile">
      <span class="stat-number">{stats.local_levels}</span>
      <span class="stat-label">Local Levels Total</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-tile">
      <span class="stat-number">{stats.protected_areas}</span>
      <span class="stat-label">Protected &amp; Special Areas</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-strip">
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">🔍</div>
      <h3>Find data</h3>
      <p>Browse boundaries by administrative level, or narrow down to a single province.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">⬇️</div>
      <h3>Download in any format</h3>
      <p>Pick whatever your tool needs: GeoJSON, TopoJSON, Shapefile, KML, or GeoPackage.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">🗺️</div>
      <h3>View on the map</h3>
      <p>Explore every boundary interactively, layer by layer, before you download.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 1em;">Browse by level</h2>
  <div class="format-cards">
    <a class="format-card" href="/download/#provinces">
      <h3>Provinces</h3>
      <p>{stats.provinces} provinces covering all of Nepal, whole-country files only.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="format-card" href="/download/#districts">
      <h3>Districts</h3>
      <p>{stats.districts} districts, whole-country or split into one file per province.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="format-card" href="/download/#local-levels">
      <h3>Local Levels</h3>
      <p>{stats.local_levels} local levels plus {stats.protected_areas} protected areas, whole-country or per province.</p>
    </a>
  </div>

  <section class="wrapper content-section">
    <p>
      With the promulgation of the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_Nepal">Constitution of Nepal in 2015</a>, the country restructured into a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federalism_in_Nepal">Federal Democratic Republic</a> made up of 7
      provinces and local levels categorized as rural municipality, municipality, metropolitan, and
      sub-metropolitan. The first local elections under this new structure were held in 2017.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>LocalBoundaries</strong> brings the detailed geodata of these administrative units, plus Nepal's
      national parks and wildlife reserves, in an open and reusable format that's free to reuse in QGIS,
      ArcGIS, OpenStreetMap, Google Maps, Leaflet, or Mapbox.
    </p>
    <h2>Why LocalBoundaries</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Quickly map local authority data onto OpenStreetMap, Google Maps, Leaflet, or Mapbox.</li>
      <li>Visualize and compare local-level data across Nepal for research or reporting.</li>
      <li>Support planning, analysis, and monitoring by integrating with GIS software and libraries.</li>
      <li>See exactly where administrative lines are drawn, down to the local level.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>License</h2>
    <p>
      The datasets are licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">Creative Commons
        Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
